    {
      "id": 17845,
      "name": "The Girl With No Name",
      "username": "The_Girl_With_No_Nam",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/71e660/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2018-03-03T09:17:33.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It's a testament to &gt;G Game's skill as developers that I almost never feel like a hero is completely useless in a fight. They can always do *something*.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>However, there are those exceptions to the rule, where you just think, \"This hero is dead weight in this fight.\"</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My personal go-to example for this is Freedom Six Bunker against the Chairman. There are no ongoings to destroy, and without the extra rollout speed of the other Bunker variants (except Panzer-Buster, who has an excellent power regardless), he never actually seems to do anything.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Does anyone else know of any situations like this?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:00.498Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 17844,
      "topic_slug": "times-when-a-hero-is-straight-up-useless",
      "display_username": "The Girl With No Name",
