    {
      "id": 214924,
      "name": "Ensign53",
      "username": "Ensign53",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ensign53/{size}/1904_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-03-07T19:47:02.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I often don't even bother playing ammo. They're basically like one-shots that add a little bit of damage or damage reduction, far weaker than other heroes' comparable one-shots and mostly worse than her own other cards. But I fail to draw any guns with her pretty often.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I respectfully disagree here. If you play and use her ammo one at a time, then yes, they are like very weak oneshots.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>A lot of Expat's strategy comes from building up to a big turn. (Think a more serious Guise).&nbsp; You are going to want to keep playing guns and loading ammo until you can get an unload. Speed loading helps you to replay ammo if you either need an immediate effect or dont have much else to do, but you shouldnt hit a standstill and only play then use ammo unless you are not drawing anything else, and at that point pleanty of other heroes would feel useless , so it's unfair to think of that as a uniquely Expat problem.</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:46:14.821Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 17844,
      "topic_slug": "times-when-a-hero-is-straight-up-useless",
      "display_username": "Ensign53",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"MindWanderer\"]\n\nI often don&#39;t even bother playing ammo. They&#39;re basically like one-shots that add a little bit of damage or damage reduction, far weaker than other heroes&#39; comparable one-shots and mostly worse than her own other cards. But I fail to draw any guns with her pretty often.\n\n[/quote]\n\n&nbsp;\n\nI respectfully disagree here. If you play and use her ammo one at a time, then yes, they are like very weak oneshots.&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\nA lot of Expat&#39;s strategy comes from building up to a big turn. (Think a more serious Guise).&nbsp; You are going to want to keep playing guns and loading ammo until you can get an unload. Speed loading helps you to replay ammo if you either need an immediate effect or dont have much else to do, but you shouldnt hit a standstill and only play then use ammo unless you are not drawing anything else, and at that point pleanty of other heroes would feel useless , so it&#39;s unfair to think of that as a uniquely Expat problem.\n",
